  "solution": {
    "text": "In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, molecule, last two electrons are present in anti bonding<br />orbitals.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></msup></math><br />Removal of one electron from the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, molecule gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></math> in which the number of anti bonding electrons is one less and hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BO</mi></math> increases. Thus, removal of one electron from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> stabilises the molecule."
